//! The W25Q128JV serial flash memory, Winbond, in the 8-pin SOIC 208-mil package (package code
//! S, order code W25Q128JVSIQ): the U3 of the RP2350A Minimal board.
//!
//! The pin table was written by hand from Winbond's datasheet "W25Q128JV, 3V 128M-bit serial
//! flash memory with dual/quad SPI" (Publication Release Date August 23, 2021, Revision I, 79
//! pages, fetched on 2026-11-10 from
//! <https://www.winbond.com/resource-files/W25Q128JV%20RevI%2008232021%20Plus.pdf>): section
//! 3.1 and Figure 1a (printed page 5) for the pad numbers and 3.3 "Pin Description SOIC 208-mil,
//! WSON 6x5-mm / 8x6-mm" (printed page 5) for the names, the I/O column and the notes. The
//! datasheet writes an active-low name with a leading slash (`/CS`, `/WP`, `/HOLD`); here it is
//! a trailing `#`.
//!
//! The kinds follow the I/O column: `/CS` and `CLK` are inputs, and the four data pins are
//! bidirectional (the datasheet's "I/O": IO0 to IO3 in Quad SPI). Pad 7 is `/HOLD` or `/RESET`
//! in Standard and Dual SPI and IO3 in Quad SPI (note 2: the hold function is only there for
//! Standard and Dual SPI); the 8-pin package has no pin for a reset of its own.
//!
//! The serial interface is a `Qspi` (`std::bus`) in which the flash is the slave: `CLK` is its
//! `sclk`, `/CS` its `cs` and `IO0` to `IO3` its `io0` to `io3` (in Standard SPI, `DI` is on
//! `io0` and `DO` on `io1`), so a board joins the bus with `~`.
//!
//! What is deliberately left out: the levels, ratings and timing (the part is a boundary of the
//! design: the checks that need a number are listed as not evaluated) and the other packages.

import std::bus::{Qspi, QspiRole}

/// The W25Q128JV, a 128 Mbit (16 MB) NOR flash with a Standard, Dual and Quad SPI interface, in
/// the 8-pin SOIC 208-mil package. The pad numbers are the datasheet's pin numbers.
part W25Q128Jv {
    .designator &= "U"

    /// The serial interface: `CLK`, `/CS` and `IO0` to `IO3`.
    .qspi: Qspi
    .qspi.role &= QspiRole::Slave

    pins "SOIC-8-208mil" {
        //  pin     kind           name                 pads
        .qspi.cs   input          "CS#"                "1"
        .qspi.io1  bidirectional  "DO(IO1)"            "2"
        .qspi.io2  bidirectional  "WP#(IO2)"           "3"
        .gnd       power          "GND"                "4"
        .qspi.io0  bidirectional  "DI(IO0)"            "5"
        .qspi.sclk input          "CLK"                "6"
        .qspi.io3  bidirectional  "HOLD#/RESET#(IO3)"  "7"
        .vcc       power          "VCC"                "8"
    }

    .package: Package
    catalog w25q128jv by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
